s, and third-party gift cards. Additionally, it operates digital payment platforms; offers financial services and related products, including money transfers, bill payments, money orders, check cashing, prepaid access, co-branded credit cards, installment lending, and earned wage access; and markets lines of merchandise under private and licensed brands. The company was formerly known as Wal-Mart Stores, Inc. and changed its name to Walmart Inc. in February 2018. Walmart Inc. was founded in 1945 and is based in Bentonville, Arkansas.","employees":2100000,"website":"https://www.stock.walmart.com","country":"United States","city":"Bentonville","officers":[{"name":"Mr. John R. Furner","title":"President, CEO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. John David Rainey Jr.","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Mr. Suresh  Kumar Ph.D.","title":"Executive VP, Global CTO & Chief Development Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":14.59,"tpe":21.36,"ps":1.125,"pfcf":18.81,"peg":1.44,"pb":2.57,"ev_ebitda":10.83,"rev_growth":0.045,"eps_growth":0.09,"eps_growth_fwd":0.07005,"eps_growth_next":0.072,"div_yield":0.021,"roe":0.1246,"roa":0.0556,"de":81.66,"gross_margin":0.3557,"op_margin":0.1081,"profit_margin":0.03903,"current_ratio":1.277},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":38.28,"sector":14.59,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":44.75,"sector":21.36,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":1.332,"sector":1.125,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":137.5,"sector":18.81,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":4.12,"sector":1.44,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":9.985,"sector":2.57,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":71.65,"sector":81.66,"verdict":"In line"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":0.059,"sector":0.045,"verdict":"In line"},{"k":"eps_growth","label":"EPS growth (last qtr, y/y)","v":-0.091,"sector":0.09,"verdict":"Weak"},{"k":"